T* (Nicolo Machiavelli was born at Florence on 3rd May 1469. He was the) Tj
T* (second son of Bernardo di Nicolo Machiavelli, a lawyer of some repute,) Tj
T* (and of Bartolommea di Stefano Nelli, his wife. Both parents were) Tj
T* (members of the old Florentine nobility.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (His life falls naturally into three periods, each of which singularly) Tj
T* (enough constitutes a distinct and important era in the history of) Tj
T* (Florence. His youth was concurrent with the greatness of Florence as an) Tj
T* (Italian power under the guidance of Lorenzo de? Medici, Il Magnifico.) Tj
T* (The downfall of the Medici in Florence occurred in 1494, in which year) Tj
T* (Machiavelli entered the public service. During his official career) Tj
T* (Florence was free under the government of a Republic, which lasted) Tj
T* (until 1512, when the Medici returned to power, and Machiavelli lost his) Tj
T* (office. The Medici again ruled Florence from 1512 until 1527, when they) Tj
T* (were once more driven out. This was the period of Machiavelli?s) Tj
