T* (Although there is little recorded of the youth of Machiavelli, the) Tj
T* (Florence of those days is so well known that the early environment of) Tj
T* (this representative citizen may be easily imagined. Florence has been) Tj
T* (described as a city with two opposite currents of life, one directed by) Tj
T* (the fervent and austere Savonarola, the other by the splendour-loving) Tj
T* (Lorenzo. Savonarola?s influence upon the young Machiavelli must have) Tj
T* (been slight, for although at one time he wielded immense power over the) Tj
T* (fortunes of Florence, he only furnished Machiavelli with a subject of a) Tj
T* (gibe in _The Prince_, where he is cited as an example of an unarmed) Tj
T* (prophet who came to a bad end. Whereas the magnificence of the Medicean) Tj
T* (rule during the life of Lorenzo appeared to have impressed Machiavelli) Tj
