T* (The second period of Machiavelli?s life was spent in the service of the) Tj
T* (free Republic of Florence, which flourished, as stated above, from the) Tj
T* (expulsion of the Medici in 1494 until their return in 1512. After) Tj
T* (serving four years in one of the public offices he was appointed) Tj
T* (Chancellor and Secretary to the Second Chancery, the Ten of Liberty and) Tj
T* (Peace. Here we are on firm ground when dealing with the events of) Tj
T* (Machiavelli?s life, for during this time he took a leading part in the) Tj
T* (affairs of the Republic, and we have its decrees, records, and) Tj
T* (dispatches to guide us, as well as his own writings. A mere) Tj
T* (recapitulation of a few of his transactions with the statesmen and) Tj
T* (soldiers of his time gives a fair indication of his activities, and) Tj
T* (supplies the sources from which he drew the experiences and characters) Tj
T* (which illustrate _The Prince_.) Tj
